# ---- never commit: Protected A cadet data ----
*.xlsx
*.xls
~$*
private/

# ---- never commit: Crown copyright source artwork ----
# The poster PDF and everything derived from it. Supply your own copy locally.
ACRCCP750DA003.pdf
*.pdf
rcac_badges.zip
# Delivery archives. medals.zip is byte-identical to the extracted
# "Medals and Ribbons/" folder, so tracking both stores it twice.
medals.zip
# Air artwork delivery. The pack and preview sheets are extracted from
# A-CR-CCP-850/DA-003, so they stay out like art/*. The notes, manifest and
# extraction script carry no artwork and are tracked as the citation. The medal
# files in the folder are a copy of what went into "Medals and Ribbons/".
air badges.zip
air badges/*
!air badges/NOTES.md
!air badges/air_art_manifest.json
!air badges/extract.py
!air badges/segment.py
# Revision 2 of the same delivery, already merged into "air badges/" and
# "Medals and Ribbons/". Safe to delete; ignored so its pack can't be committed.
Air follow up.zip
Air follow up/
# Full medal delivery, 2026-09-24: 1200 dpi renders, traced emblem sources, fonts. Held
# back until its ribbons are resized, then merged into "Medals and Ribbons/".
cadet_medal_art_full.zip
cadet_medal_art_full/
# Generated packs. Note `art/*` not `art/` - git cannot re-include anything
# under an excluded DIRECTORY, so the directory itself must stay visible.
art/*
!art/Shoulder Title Kit/
# The kit's script is hand-written source and is tracked. Its PNGs are traced
# from the issued Crown copyright plate, so they stay out like the rest of the art.
art/Shoulder Title Kit/*.png

# ---- generated: rebuild with build_all.py ----
# These carry the inlined artwork, so they are both large and Crown copyright.
demo/tunic.html
demo/plate.html

# ---- python ----
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.venv/
venv/
.env

# ---- editors / os ----
.vscode/
.idea/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# local standalone copies, regenerated by build_all.py
demo/*.local.html
# artwork split out of the local pages, regenerated by build_all.py. The copies
# under docs/ ARE tracked - that is what GitHub Pages serves.
demo/tunic_art.js
demo/plate_art.js

# Static site output, regenerated by build_site.py. TRACKED on purpose: Lt Beal has
# settled that the artwork may be published as part of the tool, so these are the
# publishable build and GitHub Pages serves them from master -> /docs.
#
# That decision covers the artwork AS RENDERED IN THE TOOL. It does not cover the
# poster itself or the raw badge library, so ACRCCP750DA003.pdf, rcac_badges.zip and
# art/* stay excluded above.
